OL,3,GNEWSABritish Army chef jailed for
OL,4,Aterror-linked offences
OL,5,
OL,6,FA British Army chef who made explosives
OL,7,Fand a "homemade cannon" while promoting
OL,8,Fextreme right-wing views and talking of
OL,9,Fraising a militia has been jailed.
OL,11,FMark Broadhurst, 28, was arrested at
OL,12,FCatterick Garrison, North Yorkshire, in
OL,13,FSeptember 2024, before police later
OL,14,Ffound weapons and explosive substances
OL,15,Fat his home in Chesterfield,
OL,16,FDerbyshire.
OL,18,FOfficers found a "crude" homemade
OL,19,Fcannon, gunpowder, crossbows, bolts,
OL,20,Fsix large knives and a baseball bat
OL,21,Fwhen they searched his home and
OL,22,Fbarracks quarters.
OL,23,APub: 14-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (E) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,362,360,200,160,0,100
